{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs3PpRT3cZ1yPjGKqNrx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dependency-chain enrichment is in place in `_bootstrapper.py`, with tests in `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py`. The file runs 117 passed and 1 failed. The failure, `TestPhasePrepareSource::test_constraint_logged_when_present`, also fails on the untouched baseline, so it predates this change. I didn't commit anything.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`_dependency_chain_suffix(wi)`** renders each `why_snapshot` entry as `name==version`, then appends `str(wi.req)`, producing the agreed `\" (dependency chain: ...)\"` form.\n- **`_enrich_resolution_error(item, err)`** returns `err` unchanged for non-`Resolve` items and for top-level requirements (empty `why_snapshot`). Otherwise it returns a new exception: `ResolverException` stays `ResolverException`, `RuntimeError` stays `RuntimeError`, and anything else becomes `RuntimeError(\"<TypeName>: <msg><suffix>\")`.\n- **`_handle_phase_error()`** enriches the `Resolve` error before the test-mode and multiple-versions recording, so both record the chained message. The normal-mode path now does `raise err` with no `from`, so the original is in `__context__` and `__cause__` stays unset.\n\n**Choices I made**\n\n- The normal-mode `Resolve` branch uses `raise err` instead of a bare `raise`, because a bare `raise` would re-raise the original rather than the enriched object.\n- Subclasses of `ResolverException` or `RuntimeError` come back as the base class, not the subclass. The spec said \"same shape\", and reconstructing an arbitrary subclass could fail on its `__init__` signature.\n- I added a `TestDependencyChainEnrichment` class with 10 tests covering the suffix format, each type branch, the no-op cases, normal-mode raise (including `__context__`/`__cause__`), and test-mode and multiple-versions recording.\n\n**Checks**\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on both changed files. Ruff flagged one `str(err)` inside an f-string, which I fixed.\n- `mypy` is not installed in `.venv` or on PATH, so I did not run the type check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5988,"cache_read_input_tokens":119108,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5988},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc2a0099-e6d9-4171-8530-84464f215612","uuid":"b830657f-0b0a-493d-ae02-18ba270a4306","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:16:34.974Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs3Pp9q9qZdwWdYrn5S6"}
